  "description": "<p>When attempting to perform a conditional update without server managed triples using an ETag and If-Match, Fedora 6 always returns 412 - Precondition Failed.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>To recreate:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Get the Etag for a representation without server managed triples:\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n$ curl -sSI -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Accept: application/ld+json\"</span> -H 'Prefer: <span class=\"code-keyword\">return</span>=representation; omit=\"http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//fedora.info/definitions</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p><tt>/v4/repository#ServerManaged\"' <a href=\"http://example.org/fcrepo/rest/path/to/resource\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://example.org/fcrepo/rest/path/to/resource</a> | grep Etag | cut -d '/' -f 2</tt></p></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p><tt>\"6EE1808846332B561426844981C370A0\"</tt></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Get the same representation and write it to a file:\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n$ curl -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Accept: application/ld+json\"</span> -H <span class=\"code-quote\">'Prefer: <span class=\"code-keyword\">return</span>=representation; omit=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#ServerManaged\"</span>'</span> http://example.org/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/path/to/resource &gt; test.json</span></pre>\n</div></div></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Edit the file and change some RDF.</li>\n\t<li>Try and PUT it back using `If-Match`:\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n$ curl -X PUT -H <span class=\"code-quote\">'Authorization: XXX'</span> -H <span class=\"code-quote\">'Content-Type: application/ld+json'</span> -H <span class=\"code-quote\">'Prefer: handling=lenient'</span> -H <span class=\"code-quote\">'If-Match: <span class=\"code-quote\">\"6EE1808846332B561426844981C370A0\"</span>'</span> --data-binary @test.json http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//example.org/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/path/to/resource\r\n</span>\r\nRequest failed due to unspecified failed precondition</pre>\n</div></div></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>It is unclear if this is a bug in how the ETags are generated or if I'm just not providing the correct Prefer header with the PUT request.</p>",
